e replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\nwarning: in the working copy of 'AGENTS.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\ndiff --git a/.agents/skills/execute-step/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/execute-step/SKILL.md\nindex f96e6a6..50d9893 100644\n--- a/.agents/skills/execute-step/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.agents/skills/execute-step/SKILL.md\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ entry_contract:\n   mode:\n     - default\n     - repair\n+    - finish\n   intent: Assist the user's execute-step request without workflow admission.\n   input_contract:\n     required:\n@@ -80,6 +81,16 @@ report real gaps without making them PASS. Pause only an unresolved user choice.\n \n ## Method\n \n+Read the fresh task-status and select the requested mode before checking for new\n+code work. `default` implements the current step; `repair` addresses reviewed\n+findings; `finish` disposes the current step after checking its actual execution,\n+applicable review and remaining gaps. A bare invocation does not infer `finish`\n+from the absence of code changes. If the step is already executed and reviewed,\n+report `next_route: execute-step` with `next_mode: finish`; do not copy an earlier\n+review's `close-task` suggestion while the step remains open. An explicit read-only\n+request remains read-only. In `finish` mode, do not repeat implementation or tests\n+solely to perform the step disposition.\n+\n Establish the current requested work and actual scope from the user's instruction,\n existing plan and source. Runtime state is context, not permission. Read relevant\n requirements, contracts, past findings and tests. An optional snapshot can preserve\n@@ -106,26 +117,21 @@ Do not claim independent review. Existing real reviews may be referenced without\n manufacturing a new one. Record the actual outcome and remaining work; no mandatory\n complete-executed-step or complete-reviewed-step call is needed to continue.\n \n-For a requested finish/advance, inspect the latest applicable review, checks and open\n+In `finish` mode, inspect the latest applicable review, checks and open\n findings, not just a legacy completed/clean flag. If a workflow commitment is unmet,\n apply the shared rule before that action. For example: \"No applicable review pass was\n found. Finish this step while keeping review incomplete, or review first?\" After the\n-user chooses to finish, use `task` action `step` with state `finished` (or the chosen disposition),\n+user chooses to finish, or when no material deviation needs a new choice, use\n+`task` action `step` with state `finished` (or the chosen disposition),\n actual task/plan/step, decision link and remaining work; do not manufacture a clean review or call an\n old completion gate to obtain permission. Finishing alone does not authorize the next\n step or task closure. Changed plans, scope, validation and ordering use the same rule;\n necessary in-scope implementation details and management drift do not trigger it.\n \n-When the user invokes `execute-step` without a new implementation scope after a\n-clean applicable change review, and task-status still shows the current step as\n-`executed` with no finish disposition, treat this as the requested step finish.\n-The task-status `next_action: finish-step` makes this intent explicit; it is advice,\n-not a permission token or a substitute for checking the reviewed work.\n-Verify the review still covers the actual work; a Git commit alone does not change\n-the reviewed files. Record `task` action `step` with state `finished`, the current\n-task/plan/step and review reference, then read task-status again. Do not stop with\n-\"nothing to implement\" or recommend `close-task` while that step remains open.\n-An explicit status-only or read-only request remains read-only.\n+In `finish` mode, verify the review still covers the actual work; a Git commit\n+alone does not change the reviewed files. Record the current task/plan/step and\n+review reference, then read task-status again. If the disposition was not saved,\n+report that fact and do not present the step as finished.\n \n Read task-status after recording: execution, review and step disposition are separate.\n Keep historical/late results marked historical; they must not reopen closed work or\ndiff --git a/.agents/skills/review-change/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/review-change/SKILL.md\nindex 858fadd..2e75b9a 100644\n--- a/.agents/skills/review-change/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.agents/skills/review-change/SKILL.md\n@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ by a new execution record. Read back the view, not just the saved decision.\n \n Select the next route from the task-status readback, not the review verdict alone.\n When a clean change review leaves the current step `executed` without a finish\n-disposition, recommend `next_route: execute-step` for step disposition and any\n+disposition, recommend `next_route: execute-step` with `next_mode: finish` for step disposition and any\n remaining planned work. Do not recommend `close-task` as if clean review had\n finished the step. Git commit is a separate user-authorized action; review does\n not perform it or make a missing commit a reason to rewrite the review result.\ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md b/.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md\nindex 852e9cf..14cfd2b 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md\n+++ b/.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md\n@@ -103,6 +103,11 @@ recording method. Never claim the journal or legacy projection was updated when\n Non-blocking does not mean unmanaged. Use assistance `task` actions for task\n preparation, adoption, execution, tests, reviews, review disposition, explicit Git associations\n and lifecycle. Read `TASK_MANAGEMENT_API.md` for their association fields and recovery.\n+At every explicit workflow Skill invocation, reread the selected project-local\n+`SKILL.md` from disk and query the current `task-status` or `context.management`,\n+even when the same conversation invoked it earlier. Earlier Skill text and route\n+suggestions are historical context. Report a failed state query truthfully and\n+continue independent authorized work rather than treating it as a development gate.\n A new prepare allocates stable identity and a display number; a revision keeps identity.\n Adoption chooses the exact plan, initializes work position and maintains focus.\n Review is not adoption; execution is not review; user disposition is not PASS.\ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/runtime/package-lock.json b/.workflow-system/runtime/package-lock.json\nindex 44718a8..1412664 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/runtime/package-lock.json\n+++ b/.workflow-system/runtime/package-lock.json\n@@ -1,12 +1,12 @@\n {\n   \"name\": \"vibe-coding-vnext-runtime\",\n-  \"version\": \"0.23.6\",\n+  \"version\": \"0.23.7\",\n   \"lockfileVersion\": 3,\n   \"requires\": true,\n   \"packages\": {\n     \"\": {\n       \"name\": \"vibe-coding-vnext-runtime\",\n-      \"version\": \"0.23.6\",\n+      \"version\": \"0.23.7\",\n       \"dependencies\": {\n         \"yaml\": \"2.8.3\"\n       },\ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/runtime/package.json b/.workflow-system/runtime/package.json\nindex a7123a0..32d17b5 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/runtime/package.json\n+++ b/.workflow-system/runtime/package.json\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n {\n   \"name\": \"vibe-coding-vnext-runtime\",\n-  \"version\": \"0.23.6\",\n+  \"version\": \"0.23.7\",\n   \"private\": true,\n   \"type\": \"module\",\n   \"engines\": {\ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/runtime/src/host-guidance.ts b/.workflow-system/runtime/src/host-guidance.ts\nindex 34201b6..7ca183c 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/runtime/src/host-guidance.ts\n+++ b/.workflow-system/runtime/src/host-guidance.ts\n@@ -7,9 +7,9 @@ export function renderAssistanceGuidance(): string {\n     START,\n     '## vNext workflow assistance',\n     '',\n-    '- Read `.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md` and the selected `.agents/skills/<entry>/SKILL.md`. Their assistance and one-time confirmation rules supersede older workflow admission/terminal instructions; project business constraints remain effective.',\n+    '- On every explicit workflow Skill invocation, read the selected `.agents/skills/<entry>/SKILL.md` from disk again, even in an existing conversation. Read `.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md` for the shared rules. Earlier Skill contents and earlier next_route suggestions are historical context; project business constraints remain effective.',\n     '- Runtime assists recording, evidence, snapshots and lookup. Use `.workflow-system/runtime/support/assistance.mjs` and `ASSISTANCE_API.md`; no mandatory preflight, run-entry, waiver, review receipt, retry budget or legacy state repair is needed for authorized work.',\n-    '- Query `assistance.mjs task-status` or `context.management` for current task/plan/step state. The journal-backed view replaces stale CURRENT_TASK tuples; ordinary `find` pages are not state queries. `task-context --legacy` is historical only.',\n+    '- Query `assistance.mjs task-status` or `context.management` on every workflow invocation for current task/plan/step state, including a repeated invocation in the same conversation. The journal-backed view replaces stale CURRENT_TASK tuples; ordinary `find` pages are not state queries. Report a query failure without turning it into a development gate.',\n     '- Use the assistance `task` actions for prepare/adopt/execution/review/review-decision/step/git/close. Check fact persistence, association and view publication separately; normal state maintenance is not optional. Offer rebuild/link/correct/resolve/defer for unresolved management data, without replaying business work.',\n     '- Read/search/record operations, stale metadata and equivalent details already authorized need no new confirmation. Report actual service failures and continue independent authorized work; never rerun business work just to obtain a receipt.',\n     '- For a material deviation from a still-effective workflow commitment, disclose the action, gaps and concrete consequences together and ask once only if that informed choice is unresolved. Silence is not consent.',\n@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ const OLD_LINES = new Set([\n   '- 当前 workflow-system 为 vNext；命令在本仓库实际根目录执行，不使用历史绝对工作目录。',\n   '- workflow-system 技能仅使用 `.agents/skills/<entry>/SKILL.md`。',\n   '- 先读对应 SKILL.md；prepare/confirm、review 和完成校验按当前 Runtime 契约执行。',\n+  '- Run `/sync-host-guidance` and bun run gen:all.',\n   '- 软件验证：`node .workflow-system/runtime/dist/cli.js validate-contract --root .` 与 `node .workflow-system/runtime/dist/cli.js validate --root . --summary`。',\n   '- 本项目不运行旧 workflow-system 的 Bun 生成、registry 或 host 同步命令。',\n   '- 项目事实与业务验证以 `.workflow-system/PROJECT_PROFILE.yaml` 为准；业务约束和私有技能仍有效。',\ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/runtime/src/kernel.ts b/.workflow-system/runtime/src/kernel.ts\nindex 7ea5df7..402fb63 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/runtime/src/kernel.ts\n+++ b/.workflow-system/runtime/src/kernel.ts\n@@ -139,7 +139,7 @@ export const VNEXT_RUNTIME_PACKAGE_MANIFEST_RELATIVE_PATH = '.workflow-system/ru\n export const VNEXT_RUNTIME_LOCKFILE_RELATIVE_PATH = '.workflow-system/runtime/package-lock.json';\n export const VNEXT_RUNTIME_PACKAGE_NAME = 'vibe-coding-vnext-runtime';\n export const VNEXT_RUNTIME_NODE_MIN_VERSION = '>=20.0.0';\n-export const VNEXT_RUNTIME_PACKAGE_VERSION = '0.23.6';\n+export const VNEXT_RUNTIME_PACKAGE_VERSION = '0.23.7';\n \n export const RUNTIME_OPERATION_KINDS = [\n   'task-state-transaction',\ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/runtime/support/TASK_MANAGEMENT_API.md b/.workflow-system/runtime/support/TASK_MANAGEMENT_API.md\nindex 27dd32a..bf9a47d 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/runtime/support/TASK_MANAGEMENT_API.md\n+++ b/.workflow-system/runtime/support/TASK_MANAGEMENT_API.md\n@@ -68,8 +68,9 @@ management files it produces just to record that new commit's SHA.\n request selected_task. They scan the entire saved task journal, not a bounded search page.\n The response includes adopted_plan_ref, plan/steps/environment, current_step_id, execution,\n review status and findings, review decisions, actual commits, remaining work, and advisory\n-next_route/next_action. `finish-step` means the reviewed current step still needs a\n-separate work disposition; it is not an automatic finish or closure. `state_completeness`,\n+next_route/next_mode/next_action. `execute-step` with `next_mode: finish` means the\n+reviewed current step still needs a separate work disposition; it is not an\n+automatic finish or closure. `state_completeness`,\n issues and unassociated_records must be reported; unknown\n association is not evidence that a plan/decision never existed.\n \ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/runtime/support/task-management.mjs b/.workflow-system/runtime/support/task-management.mjs\nindex cc60ee2..d9296ca 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/runtime/support/task-management.mjs\n+++ b/.workflow-system/runtime/support/task-management.mjs\n@@ -313,7 +313,7 @@ export function taskView(root, input, io) {\n         else if (!currentStep.review_ref) { route = 'review-change'; nextAction = 'review-step'; }\n         else {\n           route = 'execute-step';\n-          mode = currentStep.review_status === 'clean' || ['accept', 'continue', 'finish', 'defer'].includes(currentStep.review_choice) ? null : 'repair';\n+          mode = currentStep.review_status === 'clean' || ['accept', 'continue', 'finish', 'defer'].includes(currentStep.review_choice) ? 'finish' : 'repair';\n           nextAction = mode === 'repair' ? 'repair-step' : 'finish-step';\n         }\n       } else route = 'close-task'; // Missing optional Git associations do not imply uncommitted work.\ndiff --git a/.workflow-system/vnext/DISTRIBUTION_STATE.json b/.workflow-system/vnext/DISTRIBUTION_STATE.json\nindex 5fa7cac..f64ef48 100644\n--- a/.workflow-system/vnext/DISTRIBUTION_STATE.json\n+++ b/.workflow-system/vnext/DISTRIBUTION_STATE.json\n@@ -2,9 +2,9 @@\n   \"schema_version\": 1,\n   \"kind\": \"vibe-governance-distribution-state\",\n   \"distribution_state\": \"vnext\",\n-  \"distribution_version\": \"0.23.6\",\n-  \"manifest_digest\": \"6f280aade67b5e6370437d19a936c4ec83e390aca553867a9e7d0677aaa14975\",\n-  \"installed_at\": \"2026-09-29T17:05:30.285Z\",\n+  \"distribution_version\": \"0.23.7\",\n+  \"manifest_digest\": \"735ffd2faa54d43ef639e580ad0e0e7b0d4456711029336336dc63a1cc1d8762\",\n+  \"installed_at\": \"2026-09-29T17:34:03.725Z\",\n   \"managed_files\": [\n     {\n       \"path\": \".agents/skills/bootstrap-project/SKILL.md\",\n@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".agents/skills/execute-step/SKILL.md\",\n-      \"checksum\": \"84b6dbc32829c905ea1e2a231559f8814c150bfb6cade98f8d81eb91327a0a8b\",\n+      \"checksum\": \"30361c32162518bc81e45466cfdc41224a270512f1f93d91aaa6e8bd72897faf\",\n       \"category\": \"skill\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".agents/skills/review-change/SKILL.md\",\n-      \"checksum\": \"e59a50746b7fc1f37aa2a79646a25283d5d3257992dff8d1847b9e26ca3ebd02\",\n+      \"checksum\": \"b1eb89a7c4fdc5772d799db7cbc6e5c32553d73ea0d59679fcc43bd82e578e26\",\n       \"category\": \"skill\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".workflow-system/runtime/dist/cli.js\",\n-      \"checksum\": \"eff94a9443f7314b3dc6bc3fe9f323e5bdede21fd24f5fc2f7c669e72076f1c7\",\n+      \"checksum\": \"9a57c83139f756253d735a912d12dfcf25a6c374a4dbf15fd6c67985184d780a\",\n       \"category\": \"runtime\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -78,12 +78,12 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".workflow-system/runtime/package-lock.json\",\n-      \"checksum\": \"73ddbb7a759df5c8f01f60c834f966014877ad9272afdacdeba0f865b0296b7e\",\n+      \"checksum\": \"036a6d7b8f1d2d42db705c4036758cbb0f967f60db0faf5f3c862950ca6527cf\",\n       \"category\": \"runtime\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".workflow-system/runtime/package.json\",\n-      \"checksum\": \"9e0e4e74564849d2545261e9f57dd48b79f4ed5374c7af399ca6cd266